+# Feature Specification: Input validation
+
+**Input**: Reject invalid input with a clear error when a task is added, renamed or tagged.
+
+## Requirements
+
+- **FR-001**: A title that is empty or only spaces is rejected (checked after trimming).
+- **FR-002**: A title longer than 120 characters, after trimming, is rejected.
+- **FR-003**: A priority other than `low`, `normal` or `high` is rejected.
+- **FR-004**: A tag that is empty or contains a space is rejected. On `add`, every given tag is checked.
+- **FR-005**: Applies to `add` (title, priority, tags), `rename` (new title) and `tag` (tag).
+- **FR-006**: A rejection returns a `Result` error with the new code `invalid-input`; its message says what is wrong.
+- **FR-007**: A rejection changes nothing in the list (no task added, renamed or tagged; `updatedAt` untouched).
+
+## Assumptions
+
+- Validation comes before the duplicate check; a lookup failure (`not-found`) for the task itself still comes first.
+- A tag is "empty" if it has no characters; a tag of only spaces contains a space, so it is rejected too.
+- Whitespace-only counts any whitespace for titles (trim), and only the space character for tags.
+
+## Plan / Tasks
+
+- [x] `result.ts`: add `invalid-input` to `TodoErrorCode`.
+- [x] `task.ts`: exported validators `validateTitle`, `validatePriority`, `validateTag` returning `Result`.
+- [x] `list.ts`: use them in `add`, `rename`, `tag` before any change.
+- [x] Tests in `test/list.test.ts`.
